diff --git a/docs/chat-bots.md b/docs/chat-bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..26be973
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/chat-bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Posting as a chat bot
+
+Open **Set up chat bots** in Account settings. Add a bot and copy its bot code
+into your CI secret store. Choose open rooms on the bot form, or turn on
+**Add to all open rooms** to join existing and future open rooms. Turning it off
+keeps current memberships. Room managers can also add bots to individual open
+or closed rooms from the room’s settings.
+
+```sh
+curl --fail --data-binary 'Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅' \
+  "https://chat.example.com/rooms/${ROOM_ID}/${BOT_CODE}/messages"
+```
+
+Send UTF-8 text, not a JSON object. To send multiple lines from a file, use
+`--data-binary @filename`. Success returns `201` and a `Location` header.
+`401` means the credential is invalid or inactive, `404` means the room is
+missing or inaccessible to the bot, and `422` means the text is missing or invalid.
+
+Treat the entire posting URL as a password. Use HTTPS, avoid shell tracing,
+and configure proxies and access logs not to record these paths. Deleting the
+bot revokes its code without removing its previous messages.
+
+## Bots per member
+
+Administrators can change **Bots per member** in Account settings. The default
+is 5; set it to 0 to prevent members from creating bots. Lowering the limit
+leaves existing bots in place. Deleted bots do not count, and administrators
+can create bots regardless of the limit.
+
+## Receiving webhook events
+
+Set **Webhook URL** to your public HTTP(S) endpoint. When someone selects your
+bot from the room’s @-mention menu and posts the message, Campfire sends a JSON
+POST in the background. Use HTTPS: the payload contains the bot’s posting URL.
+Clearing the field disables callbacks, not the bot’s ability to post.
+
+The `mention` event includes `author` and `room` (each with `id` and `name`), plus
+`message.id`, `message.body.text` (the command without this bot’s mentions),
+`message.body.html` (the full rich text), and `message.link`. Both `message.link`
+and `room.reply_to` are paths relative to your Campfire origin.
+
+When the bot joins an open or closed room, its webhook receives a `joined` event
+with only `event` and `room` (`id`, `name`, and `reply_to`). Re-adding the bot
+does not send a second greeting. Direct conversations never send `joined`.
+
+Return `200` with a UTF-8 `text/plain` or `text/html` body to post a reply as the
+bot. For longer-running commands, return `204` promptly and POST text to
+`room.reply_to` later. Campfire does not follow webhook redirects.
+
+## Cooldowns and suspension
+
+A bot can post 10 messages in any 10 seconds across all its rooms, including
+webhook replies. The next post is rejected and starts a 30-second cooldown.
+On `429 Too Many Requests`, wait the number of seconds in `Retry-After` before
+posting again. Five more attempts during that cooldown suspend the bot.
+
+Ten consecutive failed webhook deliveries also suspend a bot. A timeout,
+connection error, or non-`2xx` response counts as a failure; any `2xx` resets
+the streak, even if there's no reply to post.
+
+Suspended bots receive no webhooks and posting returns `403 Forbidden`. They
+keep their memberships and messages and still count toward the owner's limit.
+The bots page shows the reason. After addressing the cause, an administrator
+can choose **Reactivate** there to restore the bot with its counters reset.
diff --git a/lib/middleware/bot_message_request.rb b/lib/middleware/bot_message_request.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ab2a91c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/middleware/bot_message_request.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+module Middleware
+  class BotMessageRequest
+    def initialize(app)
+      @app = app
+    end
+
+    def call(env)
+      # Remove credentials from the path before Rails logs the incoming request.
+      if match = %r{\A(/rooms/[^/]+)/([^/]+)/messages/?\z}.match(env["PATH_INFO"])
+        env["campfire.bot_code"] = match[2]
+        env["PATH_INFO"] = "#{match[1]}/bot/messages"
+        # curl -d defaults to form encoding, but this endpoint always takes plain text.
+        env["CONTENT_TYPE"] = "text/plain" if env["REQUEST_METHOD"] == "POST"
+      end
+
+      @app.call(env)
+    end
+  end
+end
